res and the implementation now annotate `filename` as `str | os.PathLike[str] | Iterable[str | os.PathLike[str]] | None`. The body wraps the value in a tuple when it is a `str` or `os.PathLike`. The docstring has the \"It accepts a path or any iterable of paths.\" sentence and a `versionchanged:: 8.5.0` entry. The spec mentions \"both\" overloads, but `edit` has three; only the third takes `filename`, so that is the one I changed.\n- **`src/click/_termui_impl.py`**: `Editor.edit_files` takes `Iterable[str | os.PathLike[str]]`. I left the body alone: `subprocess.Popen` accepts path objects in its argument list, so the command is already built correctly.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: the entry is at the end of the `Unreleased` list, as the spec gives it.\n\nI did not run the typing check `tests/typing/typing_edit.py` because the spec's command list doesn't include it. `SPEC.md` is still untracked in the worktree, and I did not commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 2220, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 26793, "uuid": "d19a9b5c-486f-435f-acb4-04f36b583732", "ttft_stream_ms": 1925, "time_to_request_ms": 438, "first_content_frame_ms": 1926, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
